dent :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "213b2643-d369-585f-a935-32807ac38964" :question/math-academy-id "q-337657" :question/problem "Calculate the product ${I}_{3}D$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">${I}_{3}\\cdot D=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>{{field-5}}</td><td>{{field-6}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-7}}</td><td>{{field-8}}</td><td>{{field-9}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $D$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{3}\\cdot D=D=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718890 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ab69a5-5d06-516f-bb06-99e27f4bfe9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37ab69a5-5d06-516f-bb06-99e27f4bfe9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718881} :answer-field/id #uuid "57034cb0-8512-5a05-8138-9349ef0275b8" :answer-field/key "top-left" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e56d0e1-cb3b-5865-8a40-695d99e411f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e56d0e1-cb3b-5865-8a40-695d99e411f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718878} :answer-field/id #uuid "62ea1a0b-3e09-5a1a-87c6-9812ae2b7250" :answer-field/key "bottom-left" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1367fa66-7811-5b6b-8c49-872df64436f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1367fa66-7811-5b6b-8c49-872df64436f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718879} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc2d682d-6753-52fe-beb6-3cbbc855c2b6" :answer-field/key "top-right" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3c31f6f-412f-5287-8657-29a13478c61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3c31f6f-412f-5287-8657-29a13478c61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718898} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1b79614-584f-5163-b848-97b18aa9bf16" :answer-field/key "bottom-right" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718895}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adac652f-820b-5c82-b3d1-3eb2308405e7" :question/problem "Calculate $CB$ and enter its four entries.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$CB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{top-left}}</td><td>{{top-right}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{bottom-left}}</td><td>{{bottom-right}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "$C$ has ones on its diagonal and zeros elsewhere, so $C=I_2$. Both matrices are $2 \\times 2$, so the product is defined. Hence\n\n$$\nCB=I_2 B=B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor example, the first row of $C$ selects the first row of $B$: its two entries are $1\\cdot3+0\\cdot0=3$ and $1\\cdot(-2)+0\\cdot5=-2$. The second row selects the second row of $B$, giving $0$ and $5$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e89c01c-ae1d-5806-ab4a-166ee6404955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$AE=A$, because every entry of $E$ is $1$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718884} {:answer/id #uuid "837a88be-07c2-5478-8b7e-52ffccd59ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$AE=A$, because matrix multiplication is commutative for all square matrices." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718888} {:answer/id #uuid "945cef1e-46fd-5e0c-8af8-8af4d81b5b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$AE=\\begin{bmatrix}a & c \\\\ b & d\\end{bmatrix}$, because multiplication by $E$ switches rows and columns." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718889} {:answer/id #uuid "b254fb76-4b94-5168-a8c2-9444953ae1f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$AE=A$, because each column of $E$ selects the corresponding entry from each row of $A$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718891} {:answer/id #uuid "c94d1f8d-6c10-5d39-ad9c-5ce07dee3110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$AE=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & d\\end{bmatrix}$, because matrix multiplication multiplies corresponding entries." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b254fb76-4b94-5168-a8c2-9444953ae1f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$AE=A$, because each column of $E$ selects the corresponding entry from each row of $A$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718891} :answer-field/id #uuid "d25a8a3b-32ab-5b44-849f-abf8394ed439" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718896}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd99c764-104f-5b5d-906a-fed5358659d7" :question/problem "Let $a,b,c,d$ be arbitrary real numbers, and let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nA student claims that\n\n$$\nAE=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & d\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nbecause the zero entries of $E$ erase the off-diagonal entries of $A$. Which correction gives both the correct product and a valid reason for **every** choice of $a,b,c,d$?" :question/worked-solution "$E$ is the identity matrix $I_2$. Matrix multiplication uses rows of the first matrix and columns of the second; it does not multiply corresponding entries.\n\n$$\nAE=\\begin{bmatrix}a\\cdot1+b\\cdot0 & a\\cdot0+b\\cdot1 \\\\ c\\cdot1+d\\cdot0 & c\\cdot0+d\\cdot1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}=A.\n$$\n\nEach column of $E$ selects the corresponding entry from each row of $A$. Thus the off-diagonal entries $b$ and $c$ are preserved too. The student used entrywise multiplication instead. For instance, $b=1$ makes the top-right entry of $AE$ equal to $1$, contradicting the claimed zero.\n\nThe product is unchanged because of the identity matrix, not because arbitrary matrix products commute or because $E$ has ones everywhere."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d89ebd8-596a-51c9-b3ec-711087d429fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718877} {:answer/id #uuid "42d6009d-7b8d-5e5e-a600-51673eee6694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718882} {:answer/id #uuid "61e861df-78b4-513e-b3f6-72138a6454ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718885} {:answer/id #uuid "66d0cd11-2104-5573-8f26-0ddc3e0b9742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718887} {:answer/id #uuid "b37a6c2a-349e-57ea-9d60-7760b3233000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42d6009d-7b8d-5e5e-a600-51673eee6694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718882} :answer-field/id #uuid "27dc4888-8c8c-51ae-99cd-e48b8a95ddee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8b03ac8-9501-5f57-a179-6dda9aac429d" :question/problem "Calculate the product $A I_2$, given that $I_2$ is the $2 \\times 2$ identity matrix and\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Both $A$ and $I_2$ are $2 \\times 2$ matrices, so the product is defined. Multiplication by the corresponding identity matrix leaves a matrix unchanged. Therefore,\n\n$$\nA I_2=A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b489a5-2d80-5199-be4f-772009829879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719224} {:answer/id #uuid "39f10352-97dd-52cf-95d7-b87f90ef278b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719225} {:answer/id #uuid "5864610a-467b-57ee-8cc5-50126f3b415d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719228} {:answer/id #uuid "66cace4c-1a91-5a13-a20c-c4b01c892887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719231} {:answer/id #uuid "763befd9-9db2-53a9-8c91-51324d59f0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39f10352-97dd-52cf-95d7-b87f90ef278b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719225} :answer-field/id #uuid "4668dd17-5aa9-5ab1-bfc1-130f70510984" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0393b7cc-d444-549e-8e90-a0de79cc8aef" :question/problem "Calculate $MI_3$, given that $I_3$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "$I_3$ is the corresponding identity matrix. Both matrices are $3 \\times 3$, so the product is defined. Multiplication by the corresponding identity leaves every entry unchanged.\n\n$$\nMI_3=M=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db1f584-8662-5e2c